{"timestamp": "2026-10-08T03:07:27.338976+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3B_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3B", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "OFFLINE", "red_team": "OFFLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist", "proposal_text": "Excellent questions. Methodological transparency is critical.\n\nTo address your points:\n\nOur developer velocity metric uses a weighted commit scoring that normalizes for code churn and project stage. This allows us to distinguish substantive progress from superficial activity.\n\nFor data gathering, we use authenticated API polling combined with anomaly detection to filter bot activity and accurately map contributor patterns.\n\nOur testnet simulations prioritize economic exploits, specifically simulating vectors like reentrancy and flash loans. Findings are weighted by both technical severity and mainnet exploit probability.\n\nThis automated, deep analysis is precisely how we provide the supplemental capacity to scale your team's diligence efforts without sacrificing rigor.\n\nIs this level of granular, code-level verification currently a manual bottleneck for your team?"}
