{"timestamp": "2026-10-08T03:08:08.517495+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3B_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3B", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "OFFLINE", "red_team": "OFFLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy", "proposal_text": "Excellent questions. Methodological transparency is core to our process. Here are the specifics:\n\n1.  **Commit Velocity:** We use weighted commit scoring that normalizes for code churn (additions vs. deletions) and project stage (e.g., pre-mainnet build vs. post-launch maintenance). This gives a truer signal of productive development than raw counts.\n\n2.  **Data Pipeline:** Our process relies on authenticated API polling combined with anomaly detection to filter bot activity and focus on human contributor patterns. Private repos are only reviewed with explicit, granted access.\n\n3.  **Stress Testing:** We simulate key attack vectors like reentrancy and flash loans on a forked testnet. We then weight findings based on a matrix of exploit probability and potential financial impact on mainnet.\n\nThis automated analysis provides the deep technical signal you need, saving your team from this time-intensive work.\n\nIs this level of granular, code-level verification currently a manual bottleneck for your team?"}
